Z||000000||dlancer407||06-15-2001||07:32 PM||||Hi everyone;<BR>Two weeks ago I bought my first Fiero. It's a 1985 GT with the 2.8 6 cyl. engine.After I bought it I did some research on past recalls. I came across the recall for a possible engine fire in V6 models. I then called Pontiac customer service to find out if the car I have had been included and if it had been done. They could not tell me if My car had ever been fixed.They told me to take it to a local dealer and have them look at it to see if it had been done. The mechanic at the dealer told me that he did not think it had ever been done. Part of the recall is to replace the exhaust manifold on the passenger side of the engine which is great because mine is leaking now.I need to know if anyone has had this work done in the last couple of years. I'am afraid that since this car is 16 years old and has 133,000 miles on it the guys at Pontiac may damage other parts not included in the recall and want to charge me to fix stuff they break.Ex ( THE EXHAUST SYSTEM AND TRANS COOLER LINES )||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-15-2001||07:51 PM||||Links to all the recall info are in my cave. Those documents will tell you exactly what is suposed to be done durring recall.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||06-15-2001||11:16 PM||||you are right about extra cost to you due to age of car.  I just had a brake recall done and had to by a caliper because the bleading would not come out and that is not part of the rebuild or rear caliper. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Posthumane||06-16-2001||02:27 PM||||pbj, The brake recall is supposed to include any and all parts and labour needed to get the system working properly on top of the regular replacement parts. <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/86-c-16.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/86-c-16.htm</A> ||||reg||1
